     "text": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Tuple, Any\n\ndef is_valid_sudoku(board: List[List[Any]]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a given 9x9 Sudoku board is valid according to Sudoku rules.\n    A board is valid if:\n    1. Each row contains the digits 1-9 without repetition.\n    2. Each column contains the digits 1-9 without repetition.\n    3. Each of the nine 3x3 subgrids contains the digits 1-9 without repetition.\n    4. The board must be exactly 9x9 in size.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(board) != 9 or any(len(row) != 9 for row in board):\n        return False\n\n    # Check rows\n    for row in board:\n        if len(set(row)) != 9:\n            return False\n\n    # Check columns\n    for col in range(9):\n        column = [board[row][col] for row in range(9)]\n        if len(set(column)) != 9:\n            return False\n\n    # Check 3x3 subgrids\n    for row_start in range(0, 9, 3):\n        for col_start in range(0, 9, 3):\n            subgrid = []\n            for i in range(row_start, row_start + 3):\n                for j in range(col_start, col_start + 3):\n                    subgrid.append(board[i][j])\n            if len(set(subgrid)) != 9:\n                return False\n\n    return True\n```",
